<title>USA: ITT Barton to pay $262,500 to settle U.S. claims.</title>
<headline>ITT Barton to pay $262,500 to settle U.S. claims.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Justice Department said Friday that ITT Barton, a unit of ITT Industries, will pay the federal government $262,500 to settle claims that it failed to perform required tests on equipment it made for the Navy.</p>
<p>The equipment measures the level of water, sanitary waste and other liquids in holding tanks on submarines. ITT Barton informed the Defence Department it failed to perform the tests between 1988 and May, 1993 in order to save production time.</p>
<p>ITT Industries' stock rose 75 cents to $23.75 on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
</text>
